{"ref":"BDB, מִכְתָּב","hw":"מִכְתָּב","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">מִכְתָּב</span></big>  <strong>n.m.</strong> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 21:12\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.21.12\">2 Ch 21:12</a> <strong>writing</strong>;—abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 10:4\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.10.4\">Dt 10:4</a> + 5 times; cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">מִכְתַּב</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 32:16\" href=\"/Exodus.32.16\">Ex 32:16</a> + 2 times;—<br><strong>1.</strong>  = <em>hand-writing</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">וְהַמִּכְתָּב מִכְתַּב אֱלֹהִים הוּא</span> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 32:16\" href=\"/Exodus.32.16\">Ex 32:16</a>.<br><strong>2.</strong>  = thing written, <a data-ref=\"Exodus 39:30\" href=\"/Exodus.39.30\">Ex 39:30</a> (acc. cogn. c. <span dir=\"rtl\">כָּתַב</span>), <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 10:4\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.10.4\">Dt 10:4</a>; specif. a royal enactment or edict (= <span dir=\"rtl\">כְּתָב</span> <strong>4</strong>), <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 35:4\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.35.4\">2 Ch 35:4</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">כְּתָב</span>), <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 36:22\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.36.22\">36:22</a> = <a data-ref=\"Ezra 1:1\" href=\"/Ezra.1.1\">Ezr 1:1</a>; a prophetic writing <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 21:12\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.21.12\">2 Ch 21:12</a>.<br><strong>3.</strong>  in a title, <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳ לְחִזְקִיָּהוּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 38:9\" href=\"/Isaiah.38.9\">Is 38:9</a> <em>Writing of Hezekiah</em>.","next":"BDB, כִּתִּי","prev":"BDB, כְּתֹ֫בֶת"}